# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * IIS (W3SVC) is started via Start-Service, so it runs under the Windows
#     service host (services.exe), NOT PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: IIS is ALREADY RUNNING with the vulnerable config,
# so a fix must restart W3SVC (safe now - it is not PID 1) for the live checks
# to pass. Restarting the service can never kill the container.
